                <pb facs="0805" n="693" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg693"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13242: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-28T16:00:00+08:00">October 28, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 28—9:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>99. Embassy’s 93, October 26, 5 p.m.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d696-f1"/> Party of 23
                    foreign missionaries from Lanchow arrived safely in Peiping this morning. The
                    following 11 Americans were included in the party: Miss Ruth Lindstrom, Miss
                    Anna Haupberg, Mr. and Mrs. Calvin Snyder, Mr. and Mrs. Charles Notson, and Mr.
                    and Mrs. Francis Derk and their three children. Repeated to Nanking, Shanghai
                    and Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
